    {
      "title": "Cluster Architecture: Control Plane and Nodes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cluster Architecture: Control Plane and Nodes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Components",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Where",
                "Component",
                "Job"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{green:Control plane}",
                  "`kube-apiserver`",
                  "==only front door==; all talk through it"
                ],
                [
                  "{green:Control plane}",
                  "`etcd`",
                  "key-value store of all cluster state"
                ],
                [
                  "{green:Control plane}",
                  "`kube-scheduler`",
                  "picks a node for unassigned Pods"
                ],
                [
                  "{green:Control plane}",
                  "`kube-controller-manager`",
                  "control loops: actual → desired"
                ],
                [
                  "{blue:Node}",
                  "`kubelet`",
                  "keeps assigned Pods' containers running"
                ],
                [
                  "{blue:Node}",
                  "`kube-proxy`",
                  "programs Service routing rules"
                ],
                [
                  "{blue:Node}",
                  "container runtime",
                  "containerd or CRI-O runs containers"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The declarative loop",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Submit",
                    "sub": "desired state to API",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Store",
                    "sub": "in etcd",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Watch",
                    "sub": "controllers fix drift",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Bind",
                    "sub": "scheduler picks node",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Start",
                    "sub": "kubelet runs Pod",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Control plane== decides and stores; ==workers== run app Pods",
                "Only the **API server** reads and writes etcd",
                "**kubelet** reports node and Pod status to the API server"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Check and gotcha",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl get nodes",
                "kubectl get pods -n kube-system"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No etcd backup",
              "text": "Lose etcd, lose ==all cluster state==. Running Pods keep running until their node fails."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pods: The Smallest Deployable Unit",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Pods: The Smallest Deployable Unit",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Pod is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==Pod== wraps **1+ containers** with one {blue:Pod IP}",
                "Containers talk over `localhost`, can share volumes",
                "Multi-container: coupled helpers (**sidecars**)",
                "You schedule Pods, not containers",
                "Ephemeral: replaced Pod = new name, new IP",
                "{red:Never} depend on a Pod IP"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Lifecycle",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{orange:Pending}: awaiting node or pulling images",
                "{green:Running}: containers started",
                "{blue:Succeeded} / {red:Failed}: finished OK / error",
                "`restartPolicy`: ==Always==, ==OnFailure==, ==Never=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Minimal manifest",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "apiVersion: v1",
                "kind: Pod",
                "metadata:",
                "  name: web",
                "spec:",
                "  containers:",
                "  - name: web",
                "    image: nginx"
              ],
              "note": "add ports: [{containerPort: 80}] under the container"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Apply: `kubectl apply -f pod.yaml`",
                "Quick: `kubectl run web --image=nginx`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Common mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Bare Pods in production: nothing recreates them if the node dies",
                "No resource requests or limits",
                "Using the `latest` tag"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Failure states",
              "text": "==ImagePullBackOff==, ==CrashLoopBackOff==, ==Pending==: run `kubectl describe pod` and read the **Events**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "ReplicaSets and Deployments",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "ReplicaSets and Deployments",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Chain of Control",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==ReplicaSet==: keeps `spec.replicas` identical Pods running",
                "Matches Pods by `selector.matchLabels`",
                "==Deployment== adds rolling updates and rollback",
                "Pod template change = **new ReplicaSet**; old ones kept"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Deployment",
                    "sub": "updates, rollback",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ReplicaSet",
                    "sub": "keeps N Pods",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Pods",
                    "sub": "run the app",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Bare Pod vs ReplicaSet vs Deployment",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Self-healing",
                "Scaling",
                "Rolling update",
                "History"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Bare Pod",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "{red:No}"
                ],
                [
                  "ReplicaSet",
                  "{green:Yes}",
                  "{green:Yes}",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "{red:No}"
                ],
                [
                  "Deployment",
                  "{green:Yes}",
                  "{green:Yes}",
                  "{green:Yes}",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Stateless apps: use ==Deployments=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Manifest and Scaling",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "apiVersion: apps/v1",
                "kind: Deployment",
                "metadata: {name: web}",
                "spec:",
                "  replicas: 3",
                "  selector: {matchLabels: {app: web}}",
                "  template:",
                "    {metadata: {labels: {app: web}}, spec: {containers: [{name: nginx, image: nginx}]}}"
              ],
              "note": "metadata.name is required"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`kubectl create deployment web --image=nginx --replicas=3`",
                "`kubectl scale deploy web --replicas=5`",
                "Set replicas in ==Git==, not by hand-editing live objects"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Selector must match",
              "text": "`selector.matchLabels` must equal `template.metadata.labels`, or the API rejects it. The selector is ==immutable==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rolling Updates, Rollbacks and kubectl Essentials",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Rolling Updates, Rollbacks and kubectl Essentials",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Rolling Update vs Recreate",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "New ReplicaSet ==scales up==, old one scales down",
                "`maxSurge`: extra Pods allowed, default ==25%==",
                "`maxUnavailable`: Pods allowed down, default ==25%==",
                "Only a ==Pod template== change rolls out; scaling doesn't"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "RollingUpdate",
                "Recreate"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Downtime",
                  "{green:none}",
                  "{red:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Versions",
                  "both at once",
                  "old killed first"
                ],
                [
                  "Use for",
                  "default",
                  "apps needing one version"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Update, Watch, Roll Back",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Update: `set image` or `apply -f`, then `rollout status`",
                "`history` lists revisions; `undo` goes back one, `--to-revision=N` picks",
                "`rollout pause` / `resume` batch changes",
                "`revisionHistoryLimit` default ==10== old ReplicaSets"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl set image deploy/web nginx=nginx:1.27",
                "kubectl rollout status deploy/web",
                "kubectl rollout history deploy/web",
                "kubectl rollout undo deploy/web --to-revision=2"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes and Debug Order",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No readiness probe: bad image still looks successful",
                "Forgot `-n <namespace>`: wrong namespace",
                "Debugging out of order"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "get",
                    "sub": "kubectl get",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "describe",
                    "sub": "Events",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "logs",
                    "sub": "--previous after crash",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "exec",
                    "sub": "-it pod -- sh",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
